kAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fed9ae85f5d958289c7b9e4f8eabca6ec8232b3845a5da71d7298b19faa78e8f","event_uuid":"6bcbef3b-6b86-4a6a-a746-1b36fc24d6aa","position":{"commit_sha":"2657a0b41013b90c89cd820c527a496585e0c747","position":"1788763626314246001-6bcbef3b-6b86-4a6a-a746-1b36fc24d6aa"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b218c74cc04560c13aa4ed2f57d4b810c9f1cae87d88251815c46b200aff6a83","event_uuid":"d456ae22-f611-4cd9-ab1a-b397e262395c","position":{"commit_sha":"4b3646f77d06ab2387a94f9dc47e49fefc4b29ec","position":"1788763641493508001-d456ae22-f611-4cd9-ab1a-b397e262395c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"env_integration","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"A SECOND, distinct mechanism producing the same operator-visible symptom — recorded here because it was found in the same session and a fix for one will not fix the other. It may warrant its own ticket; I am not splitting it yet because I am not certain it is a defect rather than documented eventual consistency.\n\n**Observed 2026-09-05:** the local store read lags MCP writes by roughly **90 seconds**. Concretely, an agent called `edit_ticket` to tick five acceptance criteria, got `ok` back, and launched the close seconds later — the close's structural precheck refused with all five boxes reported UNTICKED. The identical read a short wait later showed 5/5 ticked, and the close then passed.\n\nSo a caller that does the right thing — write, confirm success, proceed — gets a refusal describing state that is already false by the time they read it.\n\n**Why I am not immediately calling this a bug.** The store is git-backed with auto-commit and auto-push to `sync.remote`, so an MCP-side write reaching a local CLI reader necessarily involves a push and a fetch. Some propagation delay is inherent to that design, and `docs/concurrency.md` is explicit that the store shares every write immediately in the sense of pushing, not in the sense of every reader seeing it instantly. So this may be correct-by-design and merely under-documented.\n\n**What makes it worth recording anyway.** The failure mode is indistinguishable from a real one. A precheck that says \"these criteria are unticked\" when they were ticked ninety seconds ago is telling the agent something false about their own work, and the natural responses — re-edit, re-verify, or conclude the edit silently failed — are all wrong. It is the same shape as the stale-clone defect above: a message that points at the caller's work when the actual condition is the reader's freshness.\n\n**Two things a fix could take:** a read-after-write barrier on the close path (fetch, or wait for the write's own push to land, before the precheck reads), or a precheck message that distinguishes \"unticked\" from \"unticked as of a snapshot taken at T, which may predate your edit\". The second is cheaper and would have been enough here — the agent lost a close cycle purely to an unqualified claim.\n\n**Practical guidance in the meantime**, which I am now applying myself: after an `edit_ticket` that changes anything a close precheck reads, confirm the change is visible in a fresh read before launching the close, rather than trusting the write's own `ok`. That is the same discipline the completion verifier already demands for evidence comments — write, confirm it landed, then close.","timestamp":1788621678975795765},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review passed; claimed for TDD implementation.","timestamp":1788737204179692001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fix pushed for review: Gerrit change 2733. RED oracle added in tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_completion_gate.py::test_file_impact_close_fetches_before_rejecting_stale_clone; local make verify passed before push.","timestamp":1788750599451310001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Patch set updated on Gerrit change 2733 after review findings: preserved distinct proven-absence refusal, added coverage for refreshed absence and unrefreshable clone, and reran make verify successfully.","timestamp":1788754557560888001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Rebased Gerrit change 2733 onto current origin/main after submit conflict, resolved close_precheck.py conflict preserving attached-commit evidence, reran full make verify successfully, and pushed the updated patch set for review.","timestamp":1788760669855884001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit change 2733 merged to origin/main and this worktree was refreshed to the merged commit. Closing the ticket now.","timestamp":1788763258049929001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Ticket closed after completion verification passed; classified bug as env_integration.","timestamp":1788763641493508001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788621607732673441,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"480c2ec9-ac88-4ee5-913e-89bbdc59b76f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2084-2f7d-081c-4a84"},{"link_uuid":"90b3a26d-94ee-48a7-9611-1d119a5dc6c1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fdb0-9a19-af75-415d"},{"link_uuid":"ba1043f4-06f7-4e8e-ab0e-229068a5b9ad","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3cc4-e1bd-a310-4cf1"}],"description":"## The defect\n\nThe MCP server resolves commits against its own code clone at `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code`. That\nclone is not fetched before a completion precheck, so it can lag `origin/main`. When it does, a close\nrouted through MCP for work whose commit HAS merged is refused with \"no commit references it\" — the\nprecheck cannot see a commit that demonstrably exists.\n\nObserved 2026-09-05 while closing `5310-b51f-bba6-4e61`: the MCP path could not resolve the merged\nSHAs and refused the close. The agent did NOT force it. It fell back to the local `rebar` CLI from a\nworktree that provably contained the commits, and the same close passed — which is sound, because the\nprecheck is explicitly a worktree-HEAD reachability check and the local worktree satisfied it\nhonestly.\n\n## Why this matters more than a one-off annoyance\n\nAGENTS.md directs agents to route tracker operations THROUGH the MCP server, with the local CLI as\nthe carve-out for local-code ops. So the documented primary path is the one that fails, and it fails\nprecisely on the most common case: closing a ticket shortly after its change merges. The refusal\nmessage names the ticket's evidence (\"no commit references it\") rather than the server's own staleness,\nso it reads as a defect in the work rather than in the resolver — which invites exactly the wrong\nresponse.\n\nThe correct fallback exists and worked here, but it depends on the agent knowing that the local CLI\nis legitimate for this and that the refusal was not about their commit. An agent that believed the\nrefusal would either re-push, re-verify, or reach for a bypass.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] The MCP server's commit resolution cannot silently use a stale clone: either it fetches before\n      resolving, or it detects staleness and says so. State which and why.\n- [x] A refusal caused by the server being unable to SEE a commit is distinguishable in its message\n      from a refusal caused by no commit referencing the ticket. The two are different conditions and\n      currently render identically.\n- [x] Defect-seeded: with the clone deliberately behind a merged commit, confirm the new behaviour\n      (fetch-then-resolve, or an explicit staleness error) rather than the misleading refusal. An\n      unobserved fix is not evidence.\n- [x] The legitimate local-CLI fallback is documented where an agent hitting this will find it, so the\n      recovery does not depend on someone having seen it before.\n- [x] Portability: no dependence on any single CI provider trigger.\n\n## Testing\n\n1. RED first: put the clone behind a merged commit and reproduce the current misleading refusal.\n2. Confirm a genuinely unreferenced ticket still refuses, with its own distinct message — the fix must\n   not make the real condition unreportable.\n3. Confirm a current clone still closes normally.\n\n## Provenance\n\nFound by an agent closing three merged tickets on 2026-09-05. It reported the refusal, declined to\nforce, and used the sanctioned fallback — so no damage resulted, but only because it reasoned\ncorrectly about a message that pointed the wrong way.\n\n## Completion evidence\n\n- Implemented fetch-before-resolve for stale code clones in `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py`, reusing the existing remote probe/refresh helpers and rescanning upstream refs only after local evidence is absent.\n- Added distinct freshness/staleness messaging for an unrefreshable or unknown remote state while preserving the ordinary proven-absence refusal when refresh succeeds and no commit references the ticket.\n- Added defect-seeded and regression tests in `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_completion_gate.py` for stale clone refresh, refreshed absence, and unrefreshable clone.\n- Documented the deterministic close precheck and local CLI fallback in `docs/plan-review-gate.md`.\n- Verified locally with targeted tests, `make check`, and full `make verify`; Gerrit change 2733 merged after LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2084-2f7d-081c-4a84"],["relates_to","3cc4-e1bd-a310-4cf1"],["relates_to","fdb0-9a19-af75-415d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"d1e5fdfa-c159-4f91-b948-56c3fe4d3479","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0164-3ed8-45de-4330","ticket_type":"bug","title":"The MCP server's code clone goes stale, so MCP-routed closes of recently-merged work refuse with \"no commit references it\"","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["44349f6b-bce7-4d97-b643-9e6869f22aaa","cd1bf6fd-782f-4d49-a9c0-2f9485cd0226","6c0da942-90f0-4c33-b6db-4edcc2e5758c","cef4de33-1272-41f4-b3da-92bf8ec2f639","50c30a72-da37-4cfc-8490-35dd4435f7e4","480c2ec9-ac88-4ee5-913e-89bbdc59b76f","c95b8bb2-2106-4f17-9fef-94778f4681c7","90b3a26d-94ee-48a7-9611-1d119a5dc6c1","93e204ca-afca-46b3-9c17-dccf36da72e6","ba1043f4-06f7-4e8e-ab0e-229068a5b9ad","dfd1302f-100c-4740-a6f9-f567152c7909","89cdf1d6-b72b-4bf3-939f-230ae16101e1","d1e5fdfa-c159-4f91-b948-56c3fe4d3479","6bcbef3b-6b86-4a6a-a746-1b36fc24d6aa","d456ae22-f611-4cd9-ab1a-b397e262395c"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788766130859613265,"uuid":"8ff436a9-053a-4764-8e00-688480624a03"}